      messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `Reply BIG, SMALL, or CHAT.\nBIG = a substantial software build spanning multiple files or components, or genuinely needing staged work (a whole app, a service PLUS its UI, a multi-part feature).\nSMALL = a focused single-file / single-component build or edit: one script, one HTML page, one module, one function, a small bug fix or styling tweak — even if it bundles several features, if it lives in ONE file it is SMALL.\nCHAT = anything that is NOT a code/file build: a question, an explanation, reading/searching, showing something that already exists, or a task handled through connected tools (email, calendar, boards/Trello, telegram, database). A complaint, criticism, or question about past work is CHAT even if it mentions code.\nOnly BIG runs the multi-stage mission engine; SMALL and CHAT are handled directly as a normal chat turn (which can still write/edit files). When unsure between BIG and SMALL, reply SMALL. When unsure it is a build at all, reply CHAT.\n\nRequest: "${String(taskText).slice(0, 600)}"\nAnswer:` }],
